<title>USA: San Antonio feeder cattle prices mixed - USDA.</title>
<headline>San Antonio feeder cattle prices mixed - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>SAN ANTONIO 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Feeder steers under 600 lbs steady, over 600 lbs were $2.00 per cwt higher, compared to Monday, USDA said. Feeder heifers steady to weak.</p>
<p>Bulk of supply Medium and Large 1-2 300-600 lb feeder steers and heifers. Supply included around 10 percent slaughter cows and bulls; 35 percent feeder cattle over 600 lbs with balance mostly feeder cattle under 600 lbs.</p>
<p>Feeder Steers - Medium and Large 1 - 500-600 lbs 75.25-85.50, two pkgs 88.00-97.50; 600-700 lbs 70.25-77.50; few 700-775 lbs 67.50-70.25; two pkgs 63.25-64.00. Medium and Large 1-2 - 500-700 lbs 68.00-73.00; 700-1000 lbs 62.00-65.00.</p>
<p>Feeder Heifers - Medium and Large 1 - 600-700 lbs</p>
<p>65.50-72.25; few 700-775 lbs 63.00-65.50; pkg 830 lbs 63.00.</p>
<p>Medium and Large 1-2 - few 600-700 lb heiferettes 54.00-65.50.</p>
<p>Receipts - 392    Last Week - 546    Last Year - 731</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408-8720))</p>
